{"architectures":["x64"],"id":"IntegrIT.Hackolade","latestVersion":"8.13.8","media":{"icons":[{"mimeType":"image/png","path":"media/icon.c272f297.png","priority":1,"sha256":"c272f2977f2da05b1ad0e439e872231e3628427cd270fdf68855720e0ad74a28","source":"winget-legacy"}],"screenshots":[]},"package":{"author":"IntegrIT SA/NV","copyright":"Copyright © 2016-2026 Hackolade. All rights reserved.","copyrightUrl":"https://hackolade.com/eulas.html","description":"Polyglot Data Modeling for SQL and NoSQL databases, APIs, and storage formats","documentations":[{"DocumentLabel":"Videos","DocumentUrl":"https://hackolade.com/videos.html"},{"DocumentLabel":"FAQ","DocumentUrl":"https://hackolade.com/help/FAQandtroubleshooting.html"}],"license":"Proprietary","licenseUrl":"https://hackolade.com/eulas.html","locale":"en-US","localizations":{"en-US":{"author":"IntegrIT SA/NV","copyright":"Copyright © 2016-2026 Hackolade. All rights reserved.","copyrightUrl":"https://hackolade.com/eulas.html","description":"Polyglot Data Modeling for SQL and NoSQL databases, APIs, and storage formats","documentations":[{"DocumentLabel":"Videos","DocumentUrl":"https://hackolade.com/videos.html"},{"DocumentLabel":"FAQ","DocumentUrl":"https://hackolade.com/help/FAQandtroubleshooting.html"}],"license":"Proprietary","licenseUrl":"https://hackolade.com/eulas.html","locale":"en-US","longDescription":"Hackolade Studio is an intuitive yet powerful application to perform the visually data modeling and schema design of many SQL and NoSQL databases, APIS, and storage formats.\nHackolade Studio combines the graphical representation of collections in an Entity Relationship Diagram, with the graphical representation of the JSON Schema definition of each collection in a hierarchical schema view. Together, these graphical representations provide the schema model for data-at-rest and data-in-motion, plus the documentation of that model. The application is specifically designed around the powerful nature of JSON nested sub-objects and denormalization.\nThe software facilitates the work of, and the dialog between analysts, architects, designers, developers, testers, DBAs, and operators of systems that are based on such technologies. It also can generate schema scripts and documentation in a variety of machine-readable formats (DDLs, JSON Schema, Avro, Parquet, Protobuf, ...) as well as database instances, or human-readable formats such as HTML, Markdown, and PDF reports.\nInstead of having to find data structures tacitly described in the application code, the creation of a database model helps to evaluate design options beforehand, think through the implications of different alternatives, and recognize potential hurdles before committing sizable amounts of development effort. A database model helps plan ahead, in order to minimize later rework. In the end, the modeling process accelerates development, increases quality of the application, and reduces execution risks.","name":"Hackolade","packageUrl":"https://hackolade.com/download.html","privacyUrl":"https://hackolade.com/privacy.html","publisher":"Hackolade","publisherSupportUrl":"https://hackolade.com/help/index.html","publisherUrl":"https://hackolade.com/","purchaseUrl":"https://hackolade.com/pricing.html","releaseNotes":"- Tech refresh: ElectronJS v45.2.3 (Chromium v156.0.8078.80, NodeJS v24.22.2, V8 v15.6.75.27), and related modules\n- Workgroup: added support for OAuth authentication for GitHub Server repository connections\n- MEGA: added handling of Keep Both and Replace when resolving name conflicts during reverse-engineering\n- MEGA: added reverse-engineering of Db2-zOS Not Null with Default as required columns with WITH DEFAULT\n- MEGA: enhanced reverse-engineering of GRAPHIC and VARGRAPHIC columns into DB2 for z/OS\n- BigQuery: added support for Require partition filter on tables partitioned by time-unit column or integer range\n- BigQuery: updated glob and minimatch libraries\n- BigQuery, CockroachDB, Db2, Db2 for z/OS, DeltaLake/Databricks, Glue, Hive, MariaDB, MySQL, Oracle, Redshift, SQLServer/AzureSQL, Teradata: comment out the foreign key of a deactivated relationship\n- Databricks: added support for Microsoft Entra ID or OAuth authentication code flow (PKCE)\n- Db2: ensured boolean default value false is generated when column default values are in separate statements\n- Db2 for z/OS: added support for WITH DEFAULT without a specified value in the Properties Pane, plus forward- and reverse-engineering\n- Snowflake: updated toml and follow-redirects libraries\n- SQLServer/AzureSQL, Synapse: updated Entra ID MFA access token when user-to-machine OAuth module is exposed","releaseNotesUrl":"https://hackolade.com/versionInfo/ReadMe.txt","tags":["database","db","modeling"]},"zh-CN":{"description":"涵盖 SQL 与 NoSQL 数据库、API 及存储格式的多语言数据建模","documentations":[{"DocumentLabel":"视频","DocumentUrl":"https://hackolade.com/videos.html"},{"DocumentLabel":"常见问题","DocumentUrl":"https://hackolade.com/help/FAQandtroubleshooting.html"}],"license":"专有软件","locale":"zh-CN","longDescription":"Hackolade Studio 是一款直观而强大的应用程序，用于对多种 SQL 和 NoSQL 数据库、API 及存储格式进行可视化数据建模与模式设计。\nHackolade Studio 将实体关系图中集合的图形化表示，与层次化模式视图中每个集合的 JSON Schema 定义图形化表示相结合。这些图形化表示共同构成了静态数据和动态数据的模式模型，并附带该模型的文档说明。该应用专门围绕 JSON 嵌套子对象和非规范化的强大特性进行设计。\n该软件促进了基于此类技术的系统分析师、架构师、设计师、开发人员、测试人员、数据库管理员和运维人员之间的工作协作与对话。它还能生成多种机器可读格式（DDL、JSON Schema、Avro、Parquet、Protobuf 等）的模式脚本和文档，以及数据库实例；同时支持 HTML、Markdown 和 PDF 报告等人可读格式的输出。\n通过创建数据库模型，用户无需从应用程序代码中隐式推导数据结构，即可预先评估设计方案、深入思考不同替代方案的影响，并在投入大量开发工作前识别潜在障碍。数据库模型有助于提前规划，从而最大限度减少后期返工。最终，建模过程能加速开发进度、提升应用质量并降低实施风险。","tags":["建模","数据库"]}},"longDescription":"Hackolade Studio is an intuitive yet powerful application to perform the visually data modeling and schema design of many SQL and NoSQL databases, APIS, and storage formats.\nHackolade Studio combines the graphical representation of collections in an Entity Relationship Diagram, with the graphical representation of the JSON Schema definition of each collection in a hierarchical schema view. Together, these graphical representations provide the schema model for data-at-rest and data-in-motion, plus the documentation of that model. The application is specifically designed around the powerful nature of JSON nested sub-objects and denormalization.\nThe software facilitates the work of, and the dialog between analysts, architects, designers, developers, testers, DBAs, and operators of systems that are based on such technologies. It also can generate schema scripts and documentation in a variety of machine-readable formats (DDLs, JSON Schema, Avro, Parquet, Protobuf, ...) as well as database instances, or human-readable formats such as HTML, Markdown, and PDF reports.\nInstead of having to find data structures tacitly described in the application code, the creation of a database model helps to evaluate design options beforehand, think through the implications of different alternatives, and recognize potential hurdles before committing sizable amounts of development effort. A database model helps plan ahead, in order to minimize later rework. In the end, the modeling process accelerates development, increases quality of the application, and reduces execution risks.","name":"Hackolade","packageUrl":"https://hackolade.com/download.html","privacyUrl":"https://hackolade.com/privacy.html","publisher":"Hackolade","publisherSupportUrl":"https://hackolade.com/help/index.html","publisherUrl":"https://hackolade.com/","purchaseUrl":"https://hackolade.com/pricing.html","releaseNotes":"- Tech refresh: ElectronJS v45.2.3 (Chromium v156.0.8078.80, NodeJS v24.22.2, V8 v15.6.75.27), and related modules\n- Workgroup: added support for OAuth authentication for GitHub Server repository connections\n- MEGA: added handling of Keep Both and Replace when resolving name conflicts during reverse-engineering\n- MEGA: added reverse-engineering of Db2-zOS Not Null with Default as required columns with WITH DEFAULT\n- MEGA: enhanced reverse-engineering of GRAPHIC and VARGRAPHIC columns into DB2 for z/OS\n- BigQuery: added support for Require partition filter on tables partitioned by time-unit column or integer range\n- BigQuery: updated glob and minimatch libraries\n- BigQuery, CockroachDB, Db2, Db2 for z/OS, DeltaLake/Databricks, Glue, Hive, MariaDB, MySQL, Oracle, Redshift, SQLServer/AzureSQL, Teradata: comment out the foreign key of a deactivated relationship\n- Databricks: added support for Microsoft Entra ID or OAuth authentication code flow (PKCE)\n- Db2: ensured boolean default value false is generated when column default values are in separate statements\n- Db2 for z/OS: added support for WITH DEFAULT without a specified value in the Properties Pane, plus forward- and reverse-engineering\n- Snowflake: updated toml and follow-redirects libraries\n- SQLServer/AzureSQL, Synapse: updated Entra ID MFA access token when user-to-machine OAuth module is exposed","releaseNotesUrl":"https://hackolade.com/versionInfo/ReadMe.txt","tags":["database","db","modeling"]},"schemaVersion":1,"source":"winget","versions":[{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/8.13.8/app.json","detailSha256":"2857e529a75e1e2e5aff67981b01e8c6c01b2c362e51660ef1f140a9bc4f82dc","releaseDate":"2026-11-07","releaseDateSource":"commit","version":"8.13.8"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/8.13.7/app.json","detailSha256":"7c1a36edb430a8e4fd9d82a0670026daca8a4b2cb2d742d2470d1f2122213596","releaseDate":"2026-10-23","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"8.13.7"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/8.13.6/app.json","detailSha256":"12902b04fcd3670bf515b78ea02e332ec55add4b3704e295d2377426362da314","releaseDate":"2026-10-23","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"8.13.6"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath":"versions/8.13.5/app.json","detailSha256":"8d0d312d2e1cf259cbaf95d7dc08a160fdf4482525e04887aab538758561e513","releaseDate":"2026-10-16","releaseDateSource":"manifest","version":"8.13.5"},{"architectures":["x64"],"detailPath